<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait import payments rise 3.7 pct in July.</title>
<headline>Kuwait import payments rise 3.7 pct in July.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Payments made by Kuwaiti banks to finance imports rose 3.7 percent to 126.3 million dinars in July from 121.8 million dinars in June, a Central Bank monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>The payments were 119.8 million dinars in July 1995.</p>
<p>			   Figures in millions of dinars</p>
<p>				     July	  June	July '95</p>
<p>Documentary LCs		   93.7	  81.2	86.3</p>
<p>Bills for collection	    18.4	  17.1	19.4</p>
<p>Other payment orders	    14.2	  23.4	14.1</p>
<p>The relative importance of the U.S. dollar in the financing rose to 63.4 percent in July from 61.5 in June. That of the Japanese yen rose to 5.6 percent from 4.2 percent.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in figures are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.299 dinars)</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, Kuwait newsroom +965 243 1920</p>
